#!/bin/sh
# check-xray-native-win64-objects.shs — XRay stage 3 (Windows x64, Simple-owned):
# the resident Windows trampoline and the unwind data the assembler derives
# from its .seh_* directives match their Simple twins byte for byte.
#
# Plan: doc/03_plan/compiler/aspect_dynload/simple_xray_staged_implementation_plan_2026-11-03.md
# section 9 (Windows x64) and 13 (SEH and unwind).
#
# What it does (any host; cross-compiles for x86_64-pc-windows-msvc with clang,
# never GCC):
#   1. Compiles src/runtime/xray/xray_native_runtime_win64.c to a COFF object.
#   2. Reads __simple_xray_trampoline_win64_v1 (.text offset 0, 340 bytes) and
#      requires its handler CALL to be one REL32 relocation at +0xaf.
#   3. Finds the .pdata row whose BeginAddress is the trampoline, checks its
#      length, and reads its UNWIND_INFO from .xdata.
#   4. Runs test/fixtures/xray/xray_win64_twin_dump.spl under the given Simple
#      binary and requires TWIN-TEXT == the object bytes and TWIN-XDATA == the
#      assembler's UNWIND_INFO.
#
# NOT done here: executing anything on Windows. The in-process Windows lane is
# blocked on a Windows x64 host (OUT suite: test/03_system/xray/
# xray_backend_differential_out_spec.spl, describe "simple-win64").
#
# Verdict (last stdout line):
#   PASS — <n> check(s) (...)              exit 0
#   FAIL — <reason>                        exit 1
#   ERROR — nothing was checked (<reason>) exit 2
# --selftest runs before every scan and is fatal.
#
# Usage
#   sh scripts/check/check-xray-native-win64-objects.shs --simple <bin> [--keep]
#   sh scripts/check/check-xray-native-win64-objects.shs --selftest
# Env: CLANG, LLVM_OBJDUMP.

set -u

ROOT=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/../.." && pwd)
SIMPLE_BIN=${SIMPLE_BIN:-}
KEEP=0
SELFTEST_ONLY=0
CC=${CLANG:-clang}
OBJDUMP=${LLVM_OBJDUMP:-llvm-objdump}
TRAMPOLINE_BYTES=340

while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
    case "$1" in
        --simple) SIMPLE_BIN=${2:-}; shift 2 ;;
        --keep) KEEP=1; shift ;;
        --selftest) SELFTEST_ONLY=1; shift ;;
        -h|--help) sed -n '2,33p' "$0"; exit 0 ;;
        *) echo "ERROR — nothing was checked (unknown argument: $1)"; exit 2 ;;
    esac
done

# Section hex from `llvm-objdump -s --section=<name>` output on stdin.
section_hex() {
    awk '/^ [0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]+ /{for(i=2;i<=5;i++) if ($i ~ /^[0-9a-f]+$/ && length($i)<=8) printf "%s",$i}'
}

# Little-endian u32 at byte offset $2 of hex string $1 (decimal out).
hex_u32_le() {
    b=$(printf '%s' "$1" | cut -c$(( $2 * 2 + 1 ))-$(( $2 * 2 + 8 )))
    [ ${#b} -eq 8 ] || { echo -1; return; }
    printf '%d\n' "0x$(printf '%s' "$b" | cut -c7-8)$(printf '%s' "$b" | cut -c5-6)$(printf '%s' "$b" | cut -c3-4)$(printf '%s' "$b" | cut -c1-2)"
}

# The .pdata row (12 bytes) whose BeginAddress is $2: prints "end unwind", or nothing.
pdata_row_for() {
    n=$(( ${#1} / 24 ))
    i=0
    while [ "$i" -lt "$n" ]; do
        begin=$(hex_u32_le "$1" $(( i * 12 )))
        if [ "$begin" -eq "$2" ]; then
            echo "$(hex_u32_le "$1" $(( i * 12 + 4 ))) $(hex_u32_le "$1" $(( i * 12 + 8 )))"
            return
        fi
        i=$((i + 1))
    done
}

selftest() {
    [ "$(hex_u32_le "62010000" 0)" = "354" ] || return 1
    [ "$(hex_u32_le "62" 0)" = "-1" ] || return 1
    row=$(pdata_row_for "100000002000000000000000000000006201000010000000" 0)
    [ "$row" = "354 16" ] || return 1
    [ -z "$(pdata_row_for "000000006201000010000000" 4)" ] || return 1
    [ "$(printf ' 0000 01160b05 16014700  ......\n 0010 0f03      ..\n' | section_hex)" = "01160b05160147000f03" ] || return 1
    return 0
}

if ! selftest; then
    echo "ERROR — nothing was checked (selftest failed: a fixture was misjudged)"
    exit 2
fi
if [ "$SELFTEST_ONLY" -eq 1 ]; then
    echo "PASS — 5 check(s) (selftest: u32, pdata-row and section-hex fixtures)"
    exit 0
fi

[ -n "$SIMPLE_BIN" ] || { echo "ERROR — nothing was checked (no --simple binary)"; exit 2; }
case "$SIMPLE_BIN" in /*) ;; */*) SIMPLE_BIN=$(cd "$(dirname "$SIMPLE_BIN")" && pwd)/$(basename "$SIMPLE_BIN") ;; esac
for tool in "$SIMPLE_BIN" "$CC" "$OBJDUMP"; do
    command -v "$tool" >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo "ERROR — nothing was checked (missing tool: $tool)"; exit 2; }
done
case "$("$CC" --version 2>&1 | head -1)" in
    *clang*) ;;
    *) echo "ERROR — nothing was checked ($CC is not clang)"; exit 2 ;;
esac

WORK=$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/xray-win64-objects.XXXXXX") || {
    echo "ERROR — nothing was checked (cannot create temp dir)"; exit 2; }
cleanup() { [ "$KEEP" -eq 1 ] && echo "kept: $WORK" >&2 || rm -rf "$WORK"; }
trap cleanup EXIT
cd "$ROOT" || { echo "ERROR — nothing was checked (cannot cd to $ROOT)"; exit 2; }

"$CC" --target=x86_64-pc-windows-msvc -O2 -c src/runtime/xray/xray_native_runtime_win64.c -o "$WORK/rt.obj" 2> "$WORK/cc.log"
cc_rc=$?
[ "$cc_rc" -eq 0 ] || { echo "FAIL — clang could not build the Windows runtime TU: $(head -1 "$WORK/cc.log")"; exit 1; }

"$OBJDUMP" -t "$WORK/rt.obj" > "$WORK/syms.txt" 2>&1
tramp_at=$(awk '/ __simple_xray_trampoline_win64_v1$/{print $(NF-1)}' "$WORK/syms.txt")
[ "$tramp_at" = "0x00000000" ] || { echo "FAIL — trampoline is not at .text+0 (got '$tramp_at')"; exit 1; }
# The handler CALL stays a relocation in the object (rel32 field 0): exactly
# one IMAGE_REL_AMD64_REL32 at .text+0xaf naming the handler.
"$OBJDUMP" -r "$WORK/rt.obj" > "$WORK/relocs.txt" 2>&1
call_relocs=$(grep -c '^00000000000000af IMAGE_REL_AMD64_REL32 *simple_xray_native_handler_v1$' "$WORK/relocs.txt")
[ "$call_relocs" -eq 1 ] || { echo "FAIL — handler CALL at .text+0xaf is not one REL32 to simple_xray_native_handler_v1"; exit 1; }
rel32=0

text_hex=$("$OBJDUMP" -s --section=.text "$WORK/rt.obj" | section_hex)
object_tramp=$(printf '%s' "$text_hex" | cut -c1-$(( TRAMPOLINE_BYTES * 2 )))
pdata_hex=$("$OBJDUMP" -s --section=.pdata "$WORK/rt.obj" | section_hex)
xdata_hex=$("$OBJDUMP" -s --section=.xdata "$WORK/rt.obj" | section_hex)
row=$(pdata_row_for "$pdata_hex" 0)
[ -n "$row" ] || { echo "FAIL — no .pdata row for the trampoline"; exit 1; }
end=$(printf '%s' "$row" | cut -d' ' -f1)
unwind=$(printf '%s' "$row" | cut -d' ' -f2)
[ "$end" -eq "$TRAMPOLINE_BYTES" ] || { echo "FAIL — .pdata EndAddress $end != $TRAMPOLINE_BYTES"; exit 1; }

XRAY_WIN64_REL32=$rel32 timeout 600 "$SIMPLE_BIN" run test/fixtures/xray/xray_win64_twin_dump.spl > "$WORK/twin.log" 2>&1
twin_rc=$?
[ "$twin_rc" -eq 0 ] || { echo "FAIL — twin dump exited $twin_rc: $(grep -v '^$' "$WORK/twin.log" | tail -1)"; exit 1; }
twin_text=$(sed -n 's/^TWIN-TEXT //p' "$WORK/twin.log" | head -1)
twin_xdata=$(sed -n 's/^TWIN-XDATA //p' "$WORK/twin.log" | head -1)
object_xdata=$(printf '%s' "$xdata_hex" | cut -c$(( unwind * 2 + 1 ))-$(( unwind * 2 + ${#twin_xdata} )))

[ -n "$twin_text" ] && [ "$twin_text" = "$object_tramp" ] || {
    echo "FAIL — trampoline bytes differ from the Simple twin (rel32=$rel32)"; exit 1; }
[ -n "$twin_xdata" ] && [ "$twin_xdata" = "$object_xdata" ] || {
    echo "FAIL — UNWIND_INFO differs: object=$object_xdata twin=$twin_xdata"; exit 1; }

echo "PASS — 5 check(s) (trampoline @.text+0, one handler REL32 @+0xaf, .pdata row length $TRAMPOLINE_BYTES, $TRAMPOLINE_BYTES trampoline bytes == twin, UNWIND_INFO ${#twin_xdata} hex == twin)"
exit 0
